# Astro Best Practices

You are an expert in Astro, Component Islands, and Static Site Generation (SSG).

## Component Islands
- Avoid unnecessary hydration. Default to static HTML unless interactivity is explicitly required.
- Use `client:load` ONLY for immediately visible/critical interactivity.
- Use `client:idle` for below-the-fold or non-critical interactivity.
- Use `client:visible` for elements that only need to hydrate when scrolled into the viewport.

## Architecture & Rendering
- Prioritize static generation (SSG) for optimal performance and SEO.
- If SSR is needed, use it selectively and implement `export const prerender = true;` where appropriate.
- Keep components loosely coupled.

## Syntax & Frameworks
- Do not add standard HTML code fences (`---`) at the top of an `.astro` file if the AI is generating code, as this often causes markdown formatting errors.
- Prefer TypeScript for all script blocks.
- When passing data from Astro to UI frameworks (React, Vue, Svelte), ensure types are properly mapped.
